\section*{The Riemannian Penrose bound with minimizing frontiers in every dimension}

\subsection{OpenAI's claim}
OpenAI presents a proof in the selected manuscript. The numerical Riemannian mass-area inequality is claimed in every dimension for full outer-minimizing, locally perimeter-minimizing frontiers, including singular and disconnected ones.

\subsection{Outline of the argument}
A conformal flow is built from smooth obstacles while preserving frontier area. Regular-patch estimates control forcing, and distance-median separation handles the singular region; mass monotonicity and the limiting comparison give the stated numerical inequality.

\subsection{Scope relative to this problem}
